SidescanTools retains its own GNU GPLv3 terms. The core Python wheel does not
include that backend. The QGIS plugin includes a reviewed CLI-only source
archive for guided setup, together with its unchanged LICENSE, upstream
attribution and THIRD_PARTY.md modification notice. Vendor artwork and GUI
resources are excluded. The project's GPL-3.0-or-later choice does not change
the vendor's existing license grant.

The canonical reviewed source is vendor/sidescantools-main. Its THIRD_PARTY.md
records local modifications dated 2026-10-19. Original vendoring commit and
earlier local modification dates are unknown. The upstream comparison commit
f4d43bf27e7413e4490a0fb57300dc60d4694805 is a comparison reference, not proof
of the original source commit. Preserve these notices when redistributing
the reviewed source.

The plugin also includes the first-party engine's source archive. It does not
bundle Python, micromamba, GMT, GDAL, numerical-library binaries or an installed
environment. Guided setup downloads its runtime and dependencies separately.
Micromamba, GMT, GDAL, NumPy, Rasterio, SciPy, scikit-image, scikit-learn, pyshp,
PyYAML and other downloaded dependencies retain their respective licenses.
